From c094328d9bd9660c3e39580795cd6d75ec61de3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:51:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 120/143] pci: sunxi: mask the INTx sources when the intx
 domain is freed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sunxi_allocate_intx_domains() unmasks all four INTx sources in
SII_INT_MASK0 at probe, but nothing ever masked them again: after a
remove the enable bits survived in hardware, and on a re-bind the SII
IRQ handler is requested (and the line unmasked at the GIC) before
sunxi_pcie_host_init() creates the new intx_domain.  An endpoint
asserting INTx in that window made the handler call
generic_handle_domain_irq(pp->intx_domain == NULL, ...) and crash --
the same class of NULL dispatch that commit bb9fec690e67 ("pci:
sunxi: propagate sunxi_allocate_intx_domains() error") closed for the
first probe.

Mask the INTx sources in sunxi_free_intx_domains(), before the domain
is removed.  This runs with clocks up on every call site: the probe
error unwind, and remove(), where the port teardown now precedes
clock gating.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-rc.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-rc.c b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-rc.c
index b49c7101c..ae22d24a3 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-rc.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-rc.c
@@ -330,6 +330,22 @@ static int sunxi_allocate_intx_domains(struct sunxi_pcie_port *pp)
 
 static void sunxi_free_intx_domains(struct sunxi_pcie_port *pp)
 {
+	struct sunxi_pcie *pci = to_sunxi_pcie_from_pp(pp);
+	u32 val;
+
+	/*
+	 * Mask the INTx sources again, mirroring the enable in
+	 * sunxi_allocate_intx_domains().  The SII IRQ handler stays
+	 * requested until devm teardown and dispatches into
+	 * pp->intx_domain, so the sources must be quiet before the
+	 * domain goes away -- and a later re-probe must not receive
+	 * INTx (from the mask left enabled by a previous bind) before
+	 * its own domain exists.
+	 */
+	val = sunxi_pcie_readl(pci, SII_INT_MASK0);
+	val &= ~INTX_RX_ASSERT_MASK;
+	sunxi_pcie_writel(val, pci, SII_INT_MASK0);
+
 	if (pp->intx_domain)
 		irq_domain_remove(pp->intx_domain);
 }
